# Product UI is BPMN-native (not generic SaaS)

`apps/web` is a **semantic BPMN 2.0 editor**. Users edit **semantics**. Layout is canonical/derived. Never sell Miro. Details: `ARCHITECTURE.md`. Catalog: `.cursor/rules/semantic-component-library.mdc`.

## Litmus test (HARD)

Every prominent element must expose a BPMN-specific capability (process, gateway, lane, compliance, XML, quality). If the screen could be a CRM, whiteboard, PM, or notes app after relabeling, the design has **FAILED**.

```
❌ "Your boards" + search + pastel cards + "Create"
✅ Process list with BPMN previews, rule findings, NL → process
```

## Forbidden product copy

Never: **board**, infinite canvas (as a promise), freeform, drag anywhere, flow buddy, cute mascot-as-brand.

Say: process, model, diagram, BPMN — never “start a board”.

## Editor chrome (HARD)

Compact left rail is **navigation into a semantic catalog**, not a shape strip.

```
❌ Clone/extend bpmn-js PaletteProvider (hand/lasso/space/connect + 10 generics; rest in Replace menu)
❌ 50-icon SAP toolbar
❌ Space Tool (create/remove space) — layout owns geometry
❌ Global connect as free Visio arrows
✅ Select, Pan, Add, then Events / Activities / Gateways / Flows / Participants / Data / Artifacts
✅ Searchable catalog + contextual + + agent — one BpmnComponentRegistry
```

Unimplemented catalog rows stay visible in search, disabled, with a reason — never hidden only inside bpmn-js.

## Domain honesty

Do not invent product entities ahead of architecture. No Draft / Published / Archived (or similar lifecycle chrome) unless those statuses exist in the domain/API.

## Tone and chrome

Strict, systemic, engineering, BPMN-native (Linear × Figma × JetBrains). Less radius, less shadow, fewer pills, dense hierarchy, mono + one accent.

## Home in 10 seconds

Must communicate: (1) real BPMN artifacts (2) quality/status (3) NL process creation (4) not a drawing tool.

## Hygiene

Delete dead UI you replace. Never `open http://` or launch the user’s OS browser.
